 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Max has been given to Louis for the day, and Louis has an anniversary cake to make for a bank's banquet. In the pastry section the two of them work, and Louis can't stop giving orders. See what you can catch.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "louis",
   "t": "Макс, быстрее! Уже пора добавлять яйца.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Луи, я делаю всё по рецепту.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "louis",
   "t": "Обычно я делаю начинку сразу.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "louis",
   "t": "Мешай равномерно, чтобы без комочков.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Сколько шоколада нужно разогреть?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "louis",
   "t": "И разогреть шоколад на водяной бане.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Хорошо, белый или темный шоколад?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "louis",
   "t": "Только белый, для логотипа банка!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "louis",
   "t": "О, телефон звонит, одну секунду.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "louis",
   "t": "Алло? Нет, сейчас я на кухне.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Луи, я закончил взбивать крем.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "louis",
   "t": "О, спасибо, отличная работа!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "louis",
   "t": "Постой, а где мой любимый нож?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я не трогал твой нож, Луи.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Here's what is going on, line by line.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "louis",
   "t": "Макс, быстрее! Уже пора добавлять яйца.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Max, faster! It is time to add the eggs.' If you want someone to hurry, say ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "louis",
   "t": "быстрее",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " to tell them to go faster.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Луи, я делаю всё по рецепту.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Louis, I am doing everything according to the recipe.' When talking about following a recipe, the word becomes ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "рецепту",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " to show you are guided by it.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "louis",
   "t": "Обычно я делаю начинку сразу.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Usually I make the filling right away.' This sweet filling for the pastry is called ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "louis",
   "t": "начинку",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", from the word for stuffing.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "louis",
   "t": "Мешай равномерно, чтобы без комочков.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Stir evenly, so there are no lumps.' Nobody wants any lumps in their bowl, so he warns against ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "louis",
   "t": "комочков",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " in the mixture.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Сколько шоколада нужно разогреть?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'How much chocolate needs to be melted?' Asking about the required quantity starts with ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Сколько",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", meaning how much or how many.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "louis",
   "t": "И разогреть шоколад на водяной бане.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And melt the chocolate in a water bath.' Making a gentle water bath uses the word ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "louis",
   "t": "бане",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", which is also a traditional steam bathhouse.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Хорошо, белый или темный шоколад?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'All right, white or dark chocolate?' Dark chocolate is simply translated as ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "темный",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", which means dark rather than black.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "louis",
   "t": "Только белый, для логотипа банка!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Only white, for the bank logo!' Because this logo belongs to a bank, it becomes ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "louis",
   "t": "банка",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " to show who owns it.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "louis",
   "t": "О, телефон звонит, одну секунду.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Oh, the phone is ringing, one second.' Just like in many other languages, the word for phone is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "louis",
   "t": "телефон",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " and it sounds almost identical.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "louis",
   "t": "Алло? Нет, сейчас я на кухне.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Hello? No, right now I am in the kitchen.' Answering an incoming call begins with ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "louis",
   "t": "Алло",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", a greeting reserved strictly for phones.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Луи, я закончил взбивать крем.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Louis, I finished whipping the cream.' Whipping up the sweet mixture uses ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "крем",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", which sounds exactly like the English equivalent.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "louis",
   "t": "О, спасибо, отличная работа!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Oh, thank you, great job!' Praising the completed work as excellent uses the word ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "louis",
   "t": "отличная",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " to show great approval.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "louis",
   "t": "Постой, а где мой любимый нож?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Wait, where is my favorite knife?' Any favourite tool or object is described as ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "louis",
   "t": "любимый",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", which is related to love.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я не трогал твой нож, Луи.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I did not touch your knife, Louis.' Denying that he touched the knife, Max uses ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "трогал",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " to say he kept his hands off. Now you can hear it all again.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "louis",
   "t": "Макс, быстрее! Уже пора добавлять яйца.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Луи, я делаю всё по рецепту.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
